01:36:00,660 --> 01:36:01,660
Appreciate your patience.

1073
01:36:01,660 --> 01:36:07,660
So this MOU has no money involved, but it's an agreement. Flock is the name of a company

1074
01:36:07,660 --> 01:36:14,660
who is growing and emerging technology with camera use. So there's a lot of subdivisions,

1075
01:36:14,660 --> 01:36:19,660
civic associations, things like that, that are putting up cameras to secure their neighborhoods.

1076
01:36:19,660 --> 01:36:25,660
And for us to have access to those cameras, we have to sign an MOU that will only be used

1077
01:36:25,660 --> 01:36:29,660
for law enforcement purposes. Reporting of crimes within that neighborhood overnight,

1078
01:36:29,660 --> 01:36:34,660
we could remote into those cameras and use it only for law enforcement purposes, and

1079
01:36:34,660 --> 01:36:39,660
we would not have a third party vendor attached at all. And that's by federal law as well.

1080
01:36:39,660 --> 01:36:44,660
So it's just a handshake agreement with a major camera manufacturer. It's part of the

1081
01:36:44,660 --> 01:36:48,660
Huntsville Guardian Program in NAMAC.

1082
01:36:48,660 --> 01:36:51,660
Thank you very much, Chief. Any discussion? Ms. Akerage?

1083
01:36:51,660 --> 01:36:56,660
