1277
01:54:02,660 --> 01:54:12,660
Even better, raise fares back to $1.50 per ride or even $2 per ride and we'd still be the cheapest public transit in Alabama.

1278
01:54:12,660 --> 01:54:14,660
Thank you again.

1279
01:54:14,660 --> 01:54:18,660
And thank you very much, Ms. Coletti.

1280
01:54:18,660 --> 01:54:21,660
That concludes our second roster of public comments.

1281
01:54:21,660 --> 01:54:24,660
Do we have any other business before the city?

1282
01:54:24,660 --> 01:54:25,660
Yes.

1283
01:54:25,660 --> 01:54:28,660
Yes, Ms. Hageridge.

1284
01:54:29,660 --> 01:54:38,660
I'd like to respond to the public comments by Mr. Price in particular.

1285
01:54:42,660 --> 01:54:47,660
The Darby case is not anything close to what just happened on Friday.

1286
01:54:48,660 --> 01:54:58,660
This council minus Mr. Meredith, I want to address the Darby defense.

1287
01:54:59,660 --> 01:55:11,660
If it were to happen again, God forbid, and the police chief who in his estimation thought that the officer

1288
01:55:11,660 --> 01:55:21,660
followed their training and the mayor also thought that it is not up to this council to review body camera.

1289
01:55:21,660 --> 01:55:32,660
It is not because all of these things do have a direct correlation to Supreme Court decisions and the justice system has to go through.

1290
01:55:32,660 --> 01:55:51,660
I would vote again today if any employee, even a trash truck driver, was accused of a crime and it was recommended that we spend $0.50 ahead from each taxpayer to get the best defense possible.

1291
01:55:51,660 --> 01:55:53,660
I would do it again today.

1292
01:55:54,660 --> 01:55:57,660
Because that's what we do for employees.

1293
01:55:57,660 --> 01:56:09,660
Any organization has to stand by their employees and use the available tools to see that the right type of justice was done.

1294
01:56:09,660 --> 01:56:13,660
Justice has been served to Mr. Darby.

1295
01:56:13,660 --> 01:56:19,660
It is not something that is up for debate again.

1296
01:56:19,660 --> 01:56:23,660
It is something that we perhaps will learn from.

1297
01:56:23,660 --> 01:56:31,660
And this event on Friday, seek first to understand before trying to be understood.

1298
01:56:31,660 --> 01:56:48,660
The event on Friday, I am going to be talking to Chief McMurray now that he has made a public statement to find out why the employee assistance program didn't catch his predilection towards violence.

1299
01:56:48,660 --> 01:56:55,660
Why the RippleWorks software didn't catch his possible predilection towards violence.

1300
01:56:55,660 --> 01:57:01,660
Because a person's character on outside of the job does affect how they can do their job.

1301
01:57:01,660 --> 01:57:14,660
I promise you I will at least look into that to find out how somebody landed up being accused of capital murder.

1302
01:57:15,660 --> 01:57:22,660
Technically he is innocent until proven guilty, but gee, the evidence is pretty darn strong.

1303
01:57:22,660 --> 01:57:43,660
Again, I would defend an employee, even if it were a police officer, if a department manager made an assertion that their defense was important enough to spend more than just the public defender or leave them out there to dry when they don't have any insurance.

1304
01:57:43,660 --> 01:57:47,660
And stand to lose everything, police officer or not.

1305
01:57:47,660 --> 01:57:59,660
And that Mr. Price was totally, it was covered time and time again, but you never called me to talk about the employee handbook.

1306
01:57:59,660 --> 01:58:02,660
It was done by the book.

1307
01:58:02,660 --> 01:58:07,660
For the public record, the extension of his employment was by the book.

1308
01:58:07,660 --> 01:58:15,660
It was later found out that he used the federal medical leave act, which apparently, which suspended his employment status.

1309
01:58:15,660 --> 01:58:18,660
So it was a pretty clever trick.

1310
01:58:18,660 --> 01:58:20,660
Who initiated that trick?

1311
01:58:20,660 --> 01:58:25,660
I don't know, but it always takes more than one person to come up with those decisions.

1312
01:58:25,660 --> 01:58:31,660
The money, every government employee is very different than a private sector employee.

1313
01:58:31,660 --> 01:58:34,660
You used to own, you used to own a business.

1314
01:58:34,660 --> 01:58:37,660
You could fire somebody at will.

1315
01:58:37,660 --> 01:58:40,660
That doesn't happen in the government at all.

1316
01:58:40,660 --> 01:58:44,660
They have to have their hearing, which is in the handbook.

1317
01:58:44,660 --> 01:58:54,660
In this hallway, this first floor, I can get you a hard copy of that employee handbook and you can see what the steps are.

1318
01:58:54,660 --> 01:59:04,660
And you can even make an appointment with Mr. Byron Thomas to understand that process and how it was followed by the book.

1319
01:59:04,660 --> 01:59:06,660
Thank you.

1320
01:59:06,660 --> 01:59:11,660
And thank you very much for your passionate response, Ms. Akeridge.

1321
01:59:11,660 --> 01:59:15,660
At this, no, unfortunately, it's not time for a dialogue.

1322
01:59:15,660 --> 01:59:19,660
Plus, we are getting very close to when we need to take a break.

1323
01:59:19,660 --> 01:59:25,660
So at this point, if there is no further business motion to adjourn by Mr.

1324
01:59:25,660 --> 01:59:32,660
Kling, we are adjourned until the next regular council meeting on January 27th, 2022.

1325
01:59:32,660 --> 01:59:33,660
Thank you.

